{"builder":"Goal: add a new zero-dependency Node.js 22+ tool `jsonl-lint` as an npm workspace under `packages/jsonl-lint/`, in one pull request that meets every acceptance line of https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102.\n\nContext: `packages/` does not exist yet. The root `package.json` already lists `packages/*` as workspaces, and its `npm test` runs `npm test --workspaces --if-present`. CI (`.github/workflows/test.yml`) runs `npm ci` and then `npm test` on Node 22, so `package-lock.json` must match the new workspace or `npm ci` fails.\n\nSteps:\n1. Create `packages/jsonl-lint/package.json` with `\"name\": \"jsonl-lint\"`, `\"type\": \"module\"`, `\"scripts\": { \"test\": \"node --test\" }`, a `\"bin\": { \"jsonl-lint\": \"bin/jsonl-lint.js\" }` entry, `\"engines\": { \"node\": \">=22\" }`, and no `dependencies` field (no devDependencies either). Plain ES modules, no build step.\n2. Create `packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js` exporting `lint(text)`. It returns an array of `{ line, error }`, one entry for every row that is not valid JSON:\n   - Split on `\\n` (also strip a trailing `\\r` per row so CRLF files work).\n   - `line` is the 1-based physical line number in the file.\n   - Skip blank lines (empty, or whitespace only). They produce no entry but still count toward line numbers.\n   - Check a final line that has no trailing newline (an unterminated or torn last row) like any other row. A trailing newline at the end of the file must not create an extra row.\n   - `error` is a string, e.g. the `JSON.parse` error message.\n   - Return `[]` when every row is valid.\n3. Create `packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js` (starting with `#!/usr/bin/env node`, and executable with `chmod +x`, committed with mode 100755). Its behaviour:\n   - Take exactly one argument, `<file>`.\n   - Read the file as UTF-8 and call `lint`.\n   - For each result, print `<file>:<line>: <error>` to stdout, where `<file>` is the argument exactly as given.\n   - Exit 1 if there were any results and 0 if none.\n   - With no argument, or when the file is missing or unreadable, print a message to stderr (nothing to stdout) and exit 2.\n   - Use `process.exitCode` or `process.exit` so the exit codes are exact.\n4. Add node:test tests under `packages/jsonl-lint/test/` (e.g. `test/lint.test.js` and `test/cli.test.js`) so that `node --test` run in the workspace finds them. Cover each of these explicitly:\n   - (a) a clean file → `[]`, and the CLI exits 0 with no output.\n   - (b) a bad middle row → exactly one entry with the correct line number, and the CLI prints `<file>:<line>: ...` and exits 1.\n   - (c) a torn last row with no trailing newline, e.g. `{\"a\":1}\\n{\"b\":` → the last line is reported.\n   - (d) blank lines are skipped, and line numbers after them stay physical (1-based).\n   - (e) exit codes: 0 for clean, 1 for bad, 2 for a missing file, 2 for no argument, with stderr non-empty in the 2 cases.\n   Drive the CLI with `child_process.spawnSync(process.execPath, [binPath, ...])`. Write temp files under `os.tmpdir()` via `fs.mkdtempSync`.\n5. Write `packages/jsonl-lint/README.md` describing usage, output format, exit codes and the `lint(text)` API.\n6. Update the root `README.md`: replace the \"No tools yet\" bullet under \"What is here\" with a bullet listing `packages/jsonl-lint` and a one-line description.\n7. Run `npm install` at the repo root so `package-lock.json` includes the new workspace, and commit the updated lockfile. Then run `npm ci && npm test` at the root and confirm everything passes. Also run the CLI by hand on a clean file, a bad file, a missing file and with no argument, and check the output and exit codes.\n8. Open one PR on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test. Its body must contain the exact line `Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102`. Wait for the `test` workflow on the PR head to finish green. If it fails, fix the cause and push to the same PR until it is green.","ve